I am almost finished with my shopping.
But I still want some colour for my flat.
I go to a flower stall.
There are very many flowers there.
I see a large bunch.
The flowers are completely yellow.
"Good morning."
"I will take this bunch," I say to the seller.
"Very gladly."
"That comes to fourteen euros," he says.
I give him a twenty-euro note.
He counts the change directly into my hand.
"Fifteen," he says and gives me a coin.
"And five makes twenty," he then says.
He gives me a five-euro note as well.
I get exactly six euros back.
"Thank you very much!" I say.
"You are welcome."
"Have a nice weekend!" the seller answers.
